The Spice Cabinet came to the 25-year-old&#8217;s defense following her vulnerable admission. &#8220;I love you sister & i’m glad you’re doing better,&#8221; a fan replied.

na it was depression im better now tho ❤️

&mdash; ice spice (@icespice) February 25, 2026

Back in August 2024, while Ice was on the Y2K! World Tour, the &#8220;Deli&#8221; rapper hopped on X Spaces to shut down Ozempic allegations and credited working out and eating healthy. (Ozempic is an FDA-approved prescription medicine for Type 2 diabetes, but also has been used for weight loss.)

“I actually came on here to talk about that real quick. I wish y’all never learned the word Ozempic,” she said. “That’s one thing I wish. Oh my God! Like, what even is Ozempic? What the f&#8212; is that? Genuinely, what is that?&#8221;

Ice Spice continued: &#8220;You lazy-a&#8211; bi&#8212;es never heard of a gym? It’s called the gym, it’s called eating healthy, it’s called being on tour. Like, what the hell? Maybe if I was sitting at home all f&#8212;ing day, it’d be easier to stay big.&#8221;

About a week later, she followed up with a post to social media showing off her workout routine. &#8220;We beatin them allegations bae,&#8221; she added in the caption, dodging the Ozempic rumors.

On the music side, Ice Spice has yet to release a single in 2026. She closed out 2025 by making her voice-acting debut in The SpongeBob Movie: Search for SquarePants and releasing the SpongeBob song &#8220;Big Guy.&#8221;
